# Lenovo Tab Pen Pro 2 keylayout for ColorOS/AOSP frameworks.
# Module overlay (tb522fu_pen_bridge): replaces the ROM's 3-group mapping with
# SIX distinct keys so every touch-strip gesture is independently dispatchable.
#
# Device observed on ColorOS port:
#   Lenovo Tab Pen Pro 2 Consumer Control / Mouse (uhid 0005:17EF:622E)
# Raw getevent samples (HID consumer usages via EV_MSC/MSC_SCAN):
#   0x0c0601 -> two-tap / two-click
#   0x0c0612 -> touch-film slide down
#   0x0c0613 -> touch-film slide up
#   0x0c0614 -> single click
#   0x0c0611 -> long press
#   0x0c0619 -> squeeze
#
# Mapping (v4.1.14; the module's SystemStylusHooks.stripGesture() must match):
#   F1 (131) single click      0x0c0614
#   F2 (132) two-click         0x0c0601
#   F3 (133) long press        0x0c0611
#   F4 (134) squeeze           0x0c0619   (same action family as long press)
#   F5 (135) slide up          0x0c0613
#   F6 (136) slide down        0x0c0612
#
# NOTE: the ROM file groups slide-up/down/click into F1, which is why every
# swipe behaved as "single click" (colour palette). SystemStylusHooks handles
# 131..136 itself, so the generic fallback mapping for 134/135 in its generic
# branch is never reached from this device.

key usage 0x0c0614   F1
key usage 0x0c0601   F2
key usage 0x0c0611   F3
key usage 0x0c0619   F4
key usage 0x0c0613   F5
key usage 0x0c0612   F6
